{
 "id": "g-gerund-infinitive",
 "title": "动名词还是不定式",
 "en": "Gerund or Infinitive",
 "group": "动词",
 "level": "B1",
 "order": 18,
 "keywords": [
  "动词 + doing",
  "动词 + to do",
  "+ doing 和 to do",
  "介词 + doing",
  "固定说法 + doing",
  "sb to do",
  "keep doing",
  "by doing",
  "without doing",
  "suggest / recommend",
  "动词后面接什么"
 ],
 "related": [
  "g-causative-verbs",
  "g-modals-requests",
  "g-perception-verbs",
  "g-phrasal-verbs"
 ],
 "markup": {
  "[[x]]": "重点形式：这个语法要你注意的词（橙底）",
  "{x}": "变化的部分：只用在 [[ ]] 里，例如 work{s}（橙底里加粗下划线）",
  "((x))": "变回原形的动词（虚线下划线）",
  "<<x>>": "信号词（圆角框）",
  "~~x~~": "错句里错的部分（删除线）"
 },
 "sections": {
  "idea": {
   "title": "一句话说清", "short": "说清",
   "text": "一个动词后面再跟一个动词时，第二个要变样子：要么 **doing**，要么 **to do**。用哪个，是**前面那个词说了算**。感觉上：doing 多说**做过的、在做的**，to do 多说**还没做、要去做的**。",
   "uses": [
    {
     "zh": "前面那个词要 doing",
     "en": "I <<enjoy>> [[work{ing}]] with this team.",
     "en_zh": "我很喜欢和这个团队一起工作。"
    },
    {
     "zh": "前面那个词要 to do",
     "en": "We <<decided>> [[to release]] on Monday.",
     "en_zh": "我们决定周一发版。"
    },
    {
     "zh": "介词后面一定是 doing",
     "en": "Thanks <<for>> [[help{ing}]] me.",
     "en_zh": "谢谢你帮我。"
    }
   ]
  },
  "doing": {
   "title": "后面跟 doing 的词", "short": "+ing",
   "text": "这些词后面的动词加 **-ing**。不用死记全部，先记最常用的一组，口诀：**喜欢做完、别躲、继续、考虑建议**。",
   "rules": [
    {
     "ending": "喜欢、介意",
     "change": "+ doing",
     "examples": [
      "[[enjoy]]",
      "[[mind]]",
      "[[can't stand]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "做完、别躲",
     "change": "+ doing",
     "examples": [
      "[[finish]]",
      "[[avoid]]",
      "[[give up]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "继续、练习",
     "change": "+ doing",
     "examples": [
      "[[keep]]",
      "[[practise]]",
      "[[carry on]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "考虑、建议",
     "change": "+ doing",
     "examples": [
      "[[consider]]",
      "[[suggest]]",
      "[[recommend]]"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "Have you <<finished>> [[test{ing}]] the new build?",
     "zh": "新版本你测完了吗？"
    },
    {
     "en": "The app <<keeps>> [[crash{ing}]] on iPad.",
     "zh": "这个 App 在 iPad 上老是崩溃。"
    },
    {
     "en": "I <<suggest>> [[wait{ing}]] until Monday.",
     "zh": "我建议等到周一。"
    }
   ]
  },
  "todo": {
   "title": "后面跟 to do 的词", "short": "+to",
   "text": "这些词大多和**「打算、希望、答应」**有关，事情还没发生，所以用 **to do**，像一支箭指向将来。",
   "rules": [
    {
     "ending": "想要、需要",
     "change": "+ to do",
     "examples": [
      "[[want]]",
      "[[need]]",
      "[[would like]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "打算、决定",
     "change": "+ to do",
     "examples": [
      "[[plan]]",
      "[[decide]]",
      "[[hope]]",
      "[[expect]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "答应、同意",
     "change": "+ to do",
     "examples": [
      "[[promise]]",
      "[[agree]]",
      "[[offer]]",
      "[[refuse]]"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ending": "做到",
     "change": "+ to do",
     "examples": [
      "[[manage]]",
      "[[afford]]",
      "[[learn]]"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I <<need>> [[to update]] my CV.",
     "zh": "我需要更新一下简历。"
    },
    {
     "en": "She <<promised>> [[to send]] the designs today.",
     "zh": "她答应今天把设计稿发过来。"
    },
    {
     "en": "We can't <<afford>> [[to miss]] this deadline.",
     "zh": "这个截止日期我们可错过不起。"
    }
   ]
  },
  "both": {
   "title": "两种都行", "short": "都行",
   "text": "有几个词后面 doing 和 to do **都可以，意思也差不多**：开始、继续、喜欢、讨厌这几个。",
   "items": [
    {
     "rule": "start / begin",
     "en": "It <<started>> [[rain{ing}]]. / It <<started>> [[to rain]].",
     "zh": "开始下雨了。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "like / love / hate",
     "en": "I <<love>> [[cook{ing}]]. / I <<love>> [[to cook]].",
     "zh": "我喜欢做饭。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "continue",
     "en": "We'll <<continue>> [[work{ing}]] on it tomorrow.",
     "zh": "我们明天接着做。"
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    "但 would like / would love 后面只能用 to do：I'd like [[to go]]，不说 I'd like going。"
   ]
  },
  "change": {
   "title": "换了就变意思", "short": "变意思",
   "text": "这几个词最调皮：跟 doing 和跟 to do **意思完全不一样**。记住：**doing 往回看（已经做过），to do 往前看（还要去做）**。",
   "pairs": [
    {
     "with": "remember to do",
     "this": {
      "meaning": "remember doing：记得做过",
      "en": "I <<remember>> [[lock{ing}]] the door."
     },
     "that": {
      "meaning": "remember to do：记得要去做",
      "en": "<<Remember>> [[to lock]] the door."
     }
    },
    {
     "with": "stop to do",
     "this": {
      "meaning": "stop doing：不再做了",
      "en": "I <<stopped>> [[drink{ing}]] coffee."
     },
     "that": {
      "meaning": "stop to do：停下来去做别的",
      "en": "I <<stopped>> [[to drink]] some coffee."
     }
    },
    {
     "with": "try to do",
     "this": {
      "meaning": "try doing：试试这个办法",
      "en": "<<Try>> [[restart{ing}]] your phone."
     },
     "that": {
      "meaning": "try to do：努力想做到",
      "en": "I <<tried>> [[to fix]] it, but I couldn't."
     }
    },
    {
     "with": "forget to do",
     "this": {
      "meaning": "forget doing：忘了做过（常用 I'll never forget）",
      "en": "I'll never <<forget>> [[meet{ing}]] you."
     },
     "that": {
      "meaning": "forget to do：忘了去做",
      "en": "I <<forgot>> [[to reply]] to his email."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  "prep": {
   "title": "介词后面一律 doing", "short": "介词",
   "text": "at、for、before、without 这类小词（介词）后面，动词**一律加 -ing**。最坑的是：有些固定说法里的 to 也是介词，后面同样用 **doing**。",
   "items": [
    {
     "rule": "be good at + doing",
     "en": "He's good <<at>> [[explain{ing}]] things.",
     "zh": "他很会把事情讲清楚。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "before / after + doing",
     "en": "Test it <<before>> [[merg{ing}]].",
     "zh": "合并之前先测一下。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "without + doing",
     "en": "She left <<without>> [[say{ing}]] goodbye.",
     "zh": "她没说再见就走了。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "固定说法里的 to：look forward to + doing",
     "en": "I'm <<looking forward to>> [[see{ing}]] you.",
     "zh": "期待见到你。"
    },
    {
     "rule": "固定说法里的 to：be used to + doing（习惯了）",
     "en": "I'm <<used to>> [[work{ing}]] late.",
     "zh": "我习惯加班了。"
    }
   ],
   "wrong": {
    "bad": "I'm looking forward to ~~hear~~ from you.",
    "good": "I'm looking forward to [[hear{ing}]] from you."
   }
  },
  "mistakes": {
   "title": "最常见的错", "short": "易错",
   "commonMistakes": [
    {
     "bad": "I enjoy ~~to work~~ from home.",
     "good": "I enjoy [[work{ing}]] from home.",
     "why": "enjoy 后面跟 doing。"
    },
    {
     "bad": "I want ~~going~~ home.",
     "good": "I want [[to go]] home.",
     "why": "want 后面跟 to do。"
    },
    {
     "bad": "Thanks for ~~help~~ me.",
     "good": "Thanks for [[help{ing}]] me.",
     "why": "介词 for 后面跟 doing。"
    },
    {
     "bad": "I look forward to ~~meet~~ you.",
     "good": "I look forward to [[meet{ing}]] you.",
     "why": "look forward to 的 to 是介词，后面跟 doing。"
    },
    {
     "bad": "Would you mind ~~to wait~~?",
     "good": "Would you mind [[wait{ing}]]?",
     "why": "mind 后面跟 doing。"
    }
   ],
   "tip": "拿不准的时候，先看前面是不是介词：是介词，就一定是 doing。"
  }
 },
 "quiz": [
  {
